 "schema": "baxy.operation-floor.v1",
 "source": "M107 (2026-10-01): the floor of an action whose every draft was refused or whose writer ran out of time. Each catalog operation has its plain clause (infinitive, then first-person past) in Spanish and English; the sentence is built only from the turn's facts: the operation, whether it was verified, failed or left uncertain, and the observed fields named below (the identity of what was acted on, a list read, a state read after). Read by the mind (baxy_mind.operation_floor) and by the App (Baxy.App.OperationFloor, embedded resource), so both say the same sentence. noSuccessFloor: a verified result whose answer is a value only its own final says (the clock, the PC's measurements) or that is not shown (a web search, owner's rule 2026-09-24). anonymous: the target is no name to say (a search query, a folder key). compositionFailures (live 2026-10-07, «⚠ (internal_code;retry_exhausted)» shown to the person): the line a composition that every draft failed leaves when no floor tells it, by what the turn was (a question still to ask, a result, anything else); the diagnostic code stays in the private log. variants: the clause (and its facts) a verified result takes by an observed field; a failure keeps the plain clause, since a state read beside it is the one that held. attempted (M116): what a failed or uncertain step attempted, said in words (the client, the side) beside its target, with its text quoted (content keys); a quiet read that failed is told by the effects it left undone (notDone).",
 "templates": {
  "es": {
   "done": "{clause}",
